# Vulnerabilities accepted for now, each with a reason and a re-review date. See ADR-018 for the full write-up.
# Review this file whenever it's touched, and at the latest by its earliest expiry date below.

# io.netty:netty-handler, shaded inside org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-client 4.2.4 under org.apache.pulsar.shade.io.netty.
# No newer pulsar-client release exists yet (4.2.4 is the latest stable; 5.0.0 is only pre-release milestones).
# The flaw is in Netty's SNI-based virtual-host routing (SniHandler): a server using it to route inbound TLS
# connections by server name can be made to fall back to a default handler on a fragmented ClientHello. Our usage
# of this shaded Netty is as a TLS client connecting to one configured Pulsar broker (notification.pulsar.service-url),
# never as an SNI-routing proxy accepting arbitrary inbound connections, so this code path is not reachable here.
# Re-review: upgrade pulsar-client once a release ships with a patched shade, or sooner if Pulsar's own usage of
# Netty's server-side SNI routing is found.
CVE-2026-75595 exp:2026-12-31

# org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on, shaded inside org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-client 4.2.4 the same way. The flaw is a
# bypass of X.509 name-constraint enforcement (a constrained sub-CA's certificate accepted for a hostname outside
# its constraint via a trailing dot). The private CA this project generates for Pulsar's own TLS
# (deploy/tls/gen-certs.sh, see ADR-017) sets no name constraints at all, so there is
# nothing for this bypass to defeat in the shipped configuration. A deployment that layers in its own constrained
# PKI for the Pulsar broker should track this separately until pulsar-client ships a patched shade.
# Re-review: upgrade pulsar-client once a release ships with a patched shade.
CVE-2026-8763 exp:2026-12-31

# org.springframework:spring-webmvc 6.2.19 (Spring Boot 3.5.16). The flaw is remote code execution through
# XsltView, which resolves an XSLT stylesheet from a path an attacker can influence. Spring only fixed it in 7.0.9;
# no 6.2.x release carries the fix, and moving to Spring Framework 7 means Spring Boot 4, which ADR-011 rolled back.
# None of the services renders server-side views: they are JSON APIs with no ViewResolver, ModelAndView or XsltView,
# so the vulnerable code is never reached. NoServerSideViewsTest fails the build if any of them is introduced, which
# would make this entry wrong. Short expiry because it is CRITICAL.
# Re-review: take a 6.2.x release with the fix as soon as one ships, or plan the Spring Boot 4 move.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-11-30
